## The Problem: Reference Equality

When you pass an object as a prop, React uses **reference equality** (`===`) to compare props. A new object literal creates a new reference every render, even if the contents are identical.

```jsx
// ❌ This creates a NEW object reference on every parent render
function Parent() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  return (
    <Child config={{ theme: "dark", size: "large" }} /> // new reference each time
  );
}
```

---

## Solutions

### 1. `useMemo` — Memoize the object
```jsx
function Parent() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  const config = useMemo(() => ({
    theme: "dark",
    size: "large"
  }), []); // only recreates when dependencies change

  return <Child config={config} />;
}
```

### 2. `React.memo` — Skip re-renders when props are equal
```jsx
// ❌ Still broken without useMemo - memo uses shallow comparison
const Child = React.memo(({ config }) => {
  return <div>{config.theme}</div>;
});
```

```jsx
// ✅ Works correctly together
const Child = React.memo(({ config }) => {
  return <div>{config.theme}</div>;
});

function Parent() {
  const config = useMemo(() => ({ theme: "dark" }), []);
  return <Child config={config} />;
}
```

### 3. Move static objects outside the component
```jsx
// ✅ Best for truly static data - same reference always
const CONFIG = { theme: "dark", size: "large" };

function Parent() {
  return <Child config={CONFIG} />;
}
```

### 4. Custom comparison with `React.memo`
```jsx
const Child = React.memo(({ config }) => {
  return <div>{config.theme}</div>;
}, (prevProps, nextProps) => {
  // return true to SKIP re-render, false to re-render
  return prevProps.config.theme === nextProps.config.theme &&
         prevProps.config.size === nextProps.config.size;
});
```

---

## Debugging Tips

```jsx
// Check what's actually changing
const Child = React.memo(({ config }) => {
  const renderCount = useRef(0);
  console.log("Render #", ++renderCount.current, config);

  return <div>{config.theme}</div>;
});

// Or use the why-did-you-render library
// npm install @welldone-software/why-did-you-render
```

---

## Quick Decision Guide

| Situation | Solution |
|-----------|----------|
| Object never changes | Move outside component |
| Object depends on props/state | `useMemo` |
| Preventing child re-renders | `React.memo` + `useMemo` |
| Complex comparison logic | `React.memo` with custom comparator |

**The root cause is always the same:** JavaScript objects are compared by reference, not value, so `{ a: 1 } === { a: 1 }` is **`false`**.
